  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Open book contract management",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Define > Business need",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN applies to central government departments, executive agencies, and non-departmental bodies (collectively referred to as 'in-scope organisations'). Open Book Contract Management (OBCM or ‘Open Book’) involves the scrutiny of a supplier’s costs and margins through the reporting of, or accessing, accounting data. Its use is often associated with managing and controlling delivery of large, high value and complex contracts. It ensures transparency with regards to supplier charges, costs and planned return.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The overall approach to OBCM includes: a decision tool to determine the optimal benefit / cost tier of OBCM application; application model to identify the proportionate sets of tools and processes for that tier, and five tools used in OBCM processes and collaborative behaviours.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations are required to make an initial assessment of the contract to determine where OBCM can be applied and to what extent. This assessment uses a tiered framework which allows OBCM to be used in a proportionate way depending on the level of risk and complexity of the contract. OBCM should be used on those contracts where the additional costs are justified by the perceived level of benefits and risk.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The needs of the contract, as well as the level of contract risk and complexity, should be assessed using a tiered framework to determine the appropriate type and level of Open Book practices that should be applied. Consideration must be given as to whether the allocated tier will deliver good benefits without being outweighed by the costs.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "assess the needs of contracts, as well as the level of risk and complexity, to determine the appropriate type and level of Open Book practices that should be applied, using a tiered framework",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "consider a proportionate set of processes and tools to be applied based on the tier allocated, using the decision tool",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that a \"commercial sense-check\" is applied so that the Open Book practices will deliver good benefits without being outweighed by the costs.",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework, including but not limited to, the following provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (which may be particularly relevant to the consideration of this PPN):",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 18: Principles of procurement",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Open book contract management",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
